Hitty

The optional herdr-core pane client draws on herdr-app's framed client and
binary-discovery implementation (herdrdev/herdr-app, Apache License 2.0).
The reference revision, source hashes, and scope of the adaptation are recorded
in docs/provenance/herdr-pane-engine.md. Hitty's modifications are described
there. The Apache License 2.0 text is included in LICENSE.

The Codex product icon in assets/icons/agents/codex-product.png is an OpenAI
mark used to identify Codex sessions. The artwork belongs to OpenAI and is
subject to OpenAI's design guidelines at https://openai.com/brand/.
Source: https://images.ctfassets.net/kftzwdyauwt9/YgXvGzKvVcDvpJGOFyroe/777616dd860276400c9c955688dce373/codex-app.png.png?w=256

The Clawd mascot in assets/icons/agents/claude-clawd.png identifies Claude
Code sessions. Hitty crops and scales Anthropic's static Clawd artwork:
https://claude.ai/images/clawd/core/Clawd-Still.png

The full-color icon in assets/icons/agents/antigravity-full-color.png belongs
to Google and identifies Google Antigravity sessions. Source and guidelines:
https://antigravity.google/press
Source asset: https://antigravity.google/assets/image/brand/antigravity-icon__full-color.png

The Qoder CLI mark in assets/icons/agents/qoder-startup.svg identifies Qoder
and Qoder CN sessions. Hitty converted the five rows of terminal blocks and
the #27BD51 color from the Qoder CLI 1.1.96 Windows startup banner into a
vector. The original mark belongs to Qoder (https://qoder.com/cli).
